WHAT WAS CHANGED
----------------

Per section 4(b) of the License, the files carry notices of modification in
their headers; in summary:

  1. Package and command renamed: `@moy-apps/agent-office`, bin `agent-office`.
     Plugin and marketplace ids renamed to `agent-office`.
  2. Config directory moved to `~/.agent-office/` (`AGENT_OFFICE_HOME` to
     override). Endpoint resolution reads `AGENT_OFFICE_URL`/`AGENT_OFFICE_TOKEN`
     first, then the upstream `AOP_URL`/`AOP_TOKEN`, then
     `~/.agent-office/endpoint.json`, then the upstream
     `~/.roving-office/endpoint.json`, so an existing setup keeps working.
     Redaction and scene variables likewise read `AGENT_OFFICE_*` first and
     `ROVING_OFFICE_*` as a fallback.
  3. gzip removed from the transport entirely. Upstream gzips bodies over 4 KiB;
     this receiver is an Atlassian Forge web trigger, which does not deliver a
     gzipped body intact. Bodies are sent as plain bytes and an NDJSON batch is
     cut into several POSTs under 200 KB (`splitBatches`, `post`).
  4. `connect` no longer mints an office: the receiver lives inside Jira and its
     token is minted there. It stores the URL and token, keeps the web trigger's
     path instead of cutting the URL to its origin, and proves the pair by sending
     one `session.start` labelled `onboarding`.
  5. The Claude Code installer defaults to settings.json hooks that name this
     package (an npm install path is stable); the plugin route stages a local
     marketplace under `~/.agent-office/` from a packed copy of the plugin
     (`lib/pack.cjs`). The Codex installer stages the same packed plugin.
  6. The hook entry is reachable as `agent-office send <harness>` as well as
     `bin/aop-send.cjs`; the plugin hook script serves both the packed layout
     and a source checkout.
  7. User-facing strings name Agent Office for Jira. Log prefixes in the OpenClaw
     plugin changed accordingly.
  8. Tests rewritten for this package (test/).
  9. The Cursor mapper no longer declares the `session.end` capability (Cursor's
     `sessionEnd` hook does not reliably run when a chat is closed), and maps
     Cursor's `aborted`, `window_close` and `user_close` end reasons.
 10. Every envelope carries `session.actor`: `AGENT_OFFICE_ACTOR`, else `actor`
     in endpoint.json (`connect --name`), else the OS user's full name or login.


